My suggestions:

1.  Your greatest enemy below minetown is a polymorph trap. You could
lose your armor instantly. So be alert and search carefully where you
walk.

2. Related to the above: I would make finding some means of magic
resistance (cloak, armor) a high priority. Sadly, this can only come
about through searching or through wishing.

3. Just stay away from cockatrices. Fight 'em with ranged attacks.
Don't touch 'em. Don't use 'em.   Don't even move if you have one in
your inventory.

4.  Have you started stashing our stuff?   Gotta stay unburdened.

5. Be ready for soldier ant attacks. This means having some means of
escape (teleport, digging, E-engraving tool) handy.

6. If you're looking for a specific suggestion after finishing Mine's
end, I would suggest either the main dungeon or Fort Ludios.
Reconnoiter the second with telepathy -- if the monsters look like you
can take 'em, there's your protection money. 

